1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,080
The longer you run a cloud code session,

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:02,960
the number it gets,

3
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,760
and using Compact is not enough to fix it.

4
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:08,400
Compacting still drags the old conversation forward,

5
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:09,920
meaning it brings the dead ends,

6
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:11,240
the messy debugging,

7
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:13,720
and all the bad assumptions in the next conversation.

8
00:00:13,720 --> 00:00:15,520
I call this context rot,

9
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:16,920
and it's killing your code.

10
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:18,960
So what you want instead is a full handoff.

11
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,960
So before you end a session,

12
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,800
tell Cloud to create a handoff.md file,

13
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:25,800
and have it include six things.

14
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:27,320
The goal, the current state,

15
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,920
active files that's working on,

16
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:30,200
any changes it made,

17
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:33,200
a list of failed attempts and specific next steps

18
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,280
that it was focused on.

19
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:36,480
Then run the forward slash clear command

20
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:37,800
or open a new session,

21
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,720
and tell it to read the handoff doc

22
00:00:39,720 --> 00:00:41,640
and continue from where it left off.

23
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,480
And you want to use this

24
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:43,880
when you're stepping away for hours,

25
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:46,840
or when Cloud keeps making the same broken mistake on a loop.

26
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:49,320
Now I made a short guide that tells you exactly how to do

27
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:50,520
this and how to get started.

28
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:51,960
Comment clear below,

29
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:53,120
and I'll send it right over.

